plugin-qualify (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The package carries the LV2 measurer taken in from openmixer,
    lv2_measure, in /usr/lib/plugin-qualify beside the CLAP prober. It
    prints what openmixer's copy prints, the plugin's integrity pin
    included.
  * lv2-measure.mjs measures the hosting dimensions (stability, rtSafety,
    features) through it, one process per plugin under the interposer;
    --plugins names the plugins without a scan.
  * The command looks for the measurer by its setting (OMX_LV2_MEASURE),
    then where the package installs it, then in the checkout's
    native/build.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000

plugin-qualify (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The package carries the CLAP prober and its interposer, in
    /usr/lib/plugin-qualify, so an installed plugin-qualify qualifies CLAP
    plugins and prints their integrity pin with nothing set. The package
    is now built per architecture.
  * The command looks for the prober by its setting, then where the
    package installs it, then in the checkout's native/build.
  * omx-clap-host, which brings omx-clap-scan, is recommended, and so is
    python3-lilv, which bookworm does not carry, so the package installs on
    bookworm.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:15:00 +0000

plugin-qualify (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The CLAP prober and the measurement interchange (v1.3) carry each
    plugin's integrity pin: the SHA-256 of the files the host loads and the
    omx-layout/1 fingerprint, computed through plugin-hostd 0.1.4's pin.h.

