plugin-qualify (0.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Each refusal the CLAP host core can answer with now carries a one-line
    description (CLAP_CORE_REFUSAL_DESCRIPTIONS), so a console can show
    what a refused plugin did wrong in plain words.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

plugin-qualify (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * plugin-qualify now checks CLAP plugins directly. It loads each .clap
    file without a display, runs it at every sample rate and sweeps every
    parameter while watching for anything unsafe on the audio thread, then
    writes a verdict for that exact binary and console. A plugin that has
    changed since it was checked is never trusted on the old verdict.
  * The verdict follows the extensions the chosen host profile really
    offers: asking for a profile with no CLAP support now reads as unknown
    instead of borrowing the OpenMixer console's answer.
  * The CLAP scan keeps parameter value names, the plugin's modules and its
    remote-control pages, so a console can show named choices and the
    plugin's own control pages.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

